# CivitAI Bulk Downloader

A professional, async multi-threaded downloader for CivitAI models with intelligent URL preprocessing, comprehensive testing, and CLI automation support.

## ✨ Features

- **🔐 API Authentication**: Full CivitAI API integration with bearer token support
- **⚡ High Performance**: Async multi-threaded downloads with configurable concurrency
- **🔄 Smart URL Processing**: Automatically converts any CivitAI URL format to proper download URLs
- **📁 Organized Downloads**: Automatic model type detection and organized folder structure
- **🎯 Progress Tracking**: Real-time progress bars with detailed download statistics
- **🛡️ Robust Error Handling**: Comprehensive retry logic and error recovery
- **🤖 CLI Automation**: Full command-line interface for scripted deployments
- **🧪 Thoroughly Tested**: 77+ tests with 96% success rate and comprehensive coverage
- **📊 CSV Management**: Batch processing with intelligent CSV file handling

## 🚀 Quick Start

### 1. Installation

Install it as a command with pip:
```bash
pip install git+https://github.com/deepratna-awale/civitai-bulk-downloader.git
```

This adds two commands, `civitai-download` (the downloader, same options as `python download.py`) and `civitai-preprocess` (the standalone URL preprocessor). `python -m civitai_downloader` works too. `config.json`, the `CSVs` folder and `downloads.log` are read from and written to the directory you run the command in.

Or run it from a clone:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/deepratna-awale/civitai-bulk-downloader.git
cd civitai-bulk-downloader
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

To use it from another Python project, add it as a dependency (for example in `requirements.txt`):
```
civitai-bulk-downloader @ git+https://github.com/deepratna-awale/civitai-bulk-downloader.git
```
and import it with `from civitai_downloader import CivitAIApiClient, FileDownloader, URLPreprocessor`.

### 2. Get Your API Key
Visit [CivitAI Account Settings](https://civitai.com/user/account) and create an API token.

### 3. Basic Usage
```bash
# Interactive mode (recommended for first-time users)
python download.py

# Same thing with the pip-installed command
civitai-download --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui --url "https://civitai.red/models/4201"

# Automated mode
python download.py --sd /path/to/stable-diffusion --api-key your-api-key

# Preprocess URLs then download
python download.py --preprocess --api-key your-api-key

# Download straight from a CivitAI URL (no CSV needed)
python download.py --url "https://civitai.red/models/4201?modelVersionId=130072" --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui
```

## 📋 Requirements

- **Python**: 3.9+ (3.11+ recommended)
- **CivitAI API Key**: Required for authentication
- **Dependencies**: Installed automatically by `pip install`, or via `pip install -r requirements.txt`
  - `aiohttp` - Async HTTP client
  - `aiofiles` - Async file operations  
  - `tqdm` - Progress bars
  - `loguru` - Advanced logging

## 🎯 Usage

### Interactive Mode
```bash
python download.py
```
The script will guide you through setup with prompts for:
- Stable Diffusion installation path
- CivitAI API key
- CSV directory location

### Command Line Interface
```bash
# Complete automation
python download.py \
  --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui \
  --csv ./my-models \
  --api-key your-civitai-api-key

# Available options
python download.py --help
```

#### CLI Arguments
| Argument | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `--sd`, `--stable-diffusion` | Stable Diffusion UI installation path | Interactive prompt |
| `--ui` | UI layout to use: `a1111`, `forge`, `reforge`, `sdnext`, `comfyui`, `fooocus`, `swarmui` | Auto-detected from `--sd` |
| `--csv`, `--csvs-dir` | Directory containing CSV files | `CSVs` |
| `--api-key` | CivitAI API key, or the name of an env var holding it (e.g. `CAI_API_KEY`) | `CAI_API_KEY` / `CIVITAI_API_KEY` env var, then `config.json`, then prompt |
| `--preprocess` | Preprocess URLs before downloading | `False` |
| `--url`, `--urls` | Download one or more models from CivitAI URLs, model IDs or names | None |
| `--url-file` | Text file with one URL/ID/name per line (`#` comments allowed) | None |
| `--ae-expression-loras` | Download the AutoExpress expression LoRAs into the LoRA folder, optionally only for some base models (`pony`, `illustrious`, `sdxl`, `sd15`, `flux`) | All when no type is given |
| `--type` | Force every `--url` download into one model type folder (e.g. `lora`) | Detected from CivitAI |
| `-o`, `--output` | Folder to save `--url` downloads into, with a subfolder per type, or the `--ui` layout if given (no `--sd` needed) | None |
| `--flat` | With `--output`, skip the per-type subfolders | `False` |
| `--no-aria2` | Use the built-in downloader even when aria2c is installed | `False` |
| `--connections` | Connections per file with aria2c (1-16) | `16` |
| `--verify` | Check SHA256 hashes against CivitAI for new downloads and before skipping existing files | `False` |
| `--resolve-only` | With `--url`, show the download URL and model info without downloading | `False` |

### Download by URL
Paste any CivitAI link straight into the CLI. Links stay on the site they were copied from: `civitai.com` links are looked up and downloaded on `civitai.com`, and `civitai.red` links on `civitai.red` (`civitai.green` links redirect to `civitai.com`). If a model isn't on that site, the other one is tried, so an NSFW model linked from `civitai.com` is still fetched from `civitai.red`. Bare model IDs and names start on `civitai.red`. The model type (checkpoint, LoRA, embedding, ...) is looked up on CivitAI and the file is saved into the matching folder from `model_paths`, using the file's real name.

```bash
# Model page (latest version)
python download.py --url "https://civitai.red/models/4201/realistic-vision" --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui

# A list of models of different types: each lands in its own folder
# (checkpoints in models/Stable-diffusion, LoRAs in models/Lora, embeddings in Embeddings, ...)
python download.py --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui --url \
  "https://civitai.red/models/4201?modelVersionId=130072" \
  "https://civitai.red/api/download/models/9208" \
  7808

# Or keep the list in a file, one per line
python download.py --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui --url-file my-models.txt

# Force the destination folder
python download.py --url "https://civitai.red/api/download/models/130072" --type lora --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui

# Save into any folder instead of the Stable Diffusion tree
# (creates ~/Downloads/models/checkpoint, ~/Downloads/models/lora, ...; add --flat to skip subfolders)
python download.py --url "https://civitai.red/models/4201/realistic-vision" --output ~/Downloads/models

# Use an API key from an exported environment variable
export CAI_API_KEY=your-civitai-api-key
python download.py --url "https://civitai.red/api/download/models/130072" -o ./models
python download.py --api-key CAI_API_KEY --url "https://civitai.red/models/4201" -o ./models

# Just show what would be downloaded
python download.py --url "https://civitai.red/models/4201/realistic-vision" --resolve-only
```

API key lookup order: `--api-key` (a literal key, or the name of an exported variable), then the `CAI_API_KEY` or `CIVITAI_API_KEY` environment variable, then `config.json`. Keys read from the environment are never written to `config.json`.

Accepted inputs: model pages (with or without the name slug), `?modelVersionId=` version links, `/api/download/models/` links (query options like `?type=Model&format=SafeTensor` are kept), `civitai.com`, `civitai.red`, `civitai.green` and `www.` links, bare model IDs, and model names. Inputs that point to the same file are only downloaded once.

Before anything downloads, the CLI lists which models are already present. A file counts as present only when its size matches CivitAI's exactly. Smaller files are re-downloaded, and an interrupted download (`<name>.part`) is resumed where it stopped. Add `--verify` to also compare SHA256 hashes. Files are written to `<name>.part` and only renamed once complete, so a half-finished file is never mistaken for a finished one. CSV downloads get the same check against the size the server reports. The command exits with a non-zero status if any URL fails, so it can be used in scripts.

### Faster downloads with aria2
When [aria2](https://aria2.github.io/) is installed, each file is downloaded over up to 16 connections at once, which is much faster for multi-GB checkpoints. Without it, the built-in downloader is used (one connection per file). Either way, up to `max_concurrent_downloads` files download at a time.

```bash
sudo apt install aria2        # Debian/Ubuntu/WSL
brew install aria2            # macOS
winget install aria2.aria2    # Windows
```

Both downloaders resume interrupted downloads and keep retrying as long as data is still arriving. A download only gives up after `retry_attempts` tries in a row make no progress. Optional `download_settings` in `config.json`:

| Setting | Meaning | Default |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `use_aria2` | `"auto"` (use aria2c if installed), `true` or `false` | `"auto"` |
| `aria2_connections` | Connections per file with aria2c | `16` |
| `timeout` | Seconds to wait for a connection | `30` |
| `read_timeout` | Seconds a transfer may stall before retrying | `300` |
| `retry_attempts` | Tries in a row without progress before giving up | `3` |

### Supported UIs
Models are saved into the folders the UI at `--sd` expects. The UI is detected from the install (e.g. a `custom_nodes` folder means ComfyUI); pass `--ui` to choose it yourself, or set `"ui": "comfyui"` in `config.json`. This applies to CSV batch downloads too.

| Type | A1111 / Forge / reForge | SD.Next | ComfyUI | Fooocus | SwarmUI |
|------|------|------|------|------|------|
| Checkpoint | `models/Stable-diffusion` | `models/Stable-diffusion` | `models/checkpoints` | `models/checkpoints` | `Models/Stable-Diffusion` |
| LoRA / LoCon / DoRA | `models/Lora` | `models/Lora` | `models/loras` | `models/loras` | `Models/Lora` |
| Embedding | `Embeddings` | `models/embeddings` | `models/embeddings` | `models/embeddings` | `Models/Embeddings` |
| VAE | `models/VAE` | `models/VAE` | `models/vae` | `models/vae` | `Models/VAE` |
| ControlNet | `models/ControlNet` | `models/control/controlnet` | `models/controlnet` | `models/controlnet` | `Models/controlnet` |
| Upscaler | `models/ESRGAN` | `models/ESRGAN` | `models/upscale_models` | `models/upscale_models` | `Models/upscale_models` |
| Anything else | `models/Other` | `models/Other` | `models/other` | `models/other` | `Models/other` |

A1111, Forge and reForge follow `model_paths` in `config.json`, so custom folders there still apply. `--ui` also accepts nicknames like `next`, `comfy` and `automatic1111`.

```bash
python download.py --sd ~/ComfyUI --url "https://civitai.red/models/4201" 7808
python download.py --sd ~/sdnext --ui next --url-file my-models.txt
```

### AutoExpress expression LoRAs
`--ae-expression-loras` downloads the optional expression LoRAs used by [AutoExpress](https://github.com/deepratna-awale/AutoExpress) into the LoRA folder of the chosen UI. With no value it fetches all of them; name one or more base models to fetch only those (`noobai`, `xl` and `sd1.5` work as aliases).

| Model type | LoRA | Trigger | Weight | Size |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Pony | [Facial Expressions (Pony v1.0)](https://civitai.red/models/541620?modelVersionId=1815859) by EauDeNoire | `cinematic expression style` | 0.6 | 435 MB |
| Illustrious / NoobAI | [Facial Expressions (Illu v1.0)](https://civitai.red/models/541620?modelVersionId=1815930) by EauDeNoire | `cinematic expression style` | 0.6 (skipped for anger) | 435 MB |
| Illustrious / NoobAI | [Face Enhancer Illustrious](https://civitai.red/models/1625070?modelVersionId=1839268) by roxin282 | none | 0.5 | 217 MB |
| SDXL | [Facial Expressions (XL v3)](https://civitai.red/models/541620?modelVersionId=761462) by EauDeNoire | `facial expression style` | 0.5 | 870 MB |
| SD1.5 | [Facial Expressions (SD1.5)](https://civitai.red/models/541620?modelVersionId=715217) by EauDeNoire | `facial expression style` | 0.6 | 288 MB |
| Flux | [Expression Helper 2.0](https://civitai.red/models/914282?modelVersionId=1023284) by Lara_De_Martin | none | 0.8 | 73 MB |

```bash
civitai-download --sd ~/ComfyUI --ae-expression-loras
civitai-download --ae-expression-loras pony illustrious --sd ~/stable-diffusion-webui
civitai-download --ae-expression-loras sdxl -o ./models --ui forge
```

Files keep their CivitAI names, which AutoExpress recognizes. The list is a copy of `autoexpress_core/resources/expression_loras.json` from AutoExpress, bundled at `civitai_downloader/resources/expression_loras.json`.

### URL Preprocessing
Convert any CivitAI URL format to proper download URLs:

```bash
# Standalone preprocessing
python preprocess.py --api-key your-api-key

# Preprocess specific file
python preprocess.py --file CSVs/checkpoint.csv --api-key your-api-key

# Preprocess then download
python download.py --preprocess --api-key your-api-key
```

**Supported URL Formats:**
- ✅ `https://civitai.com/api/download/models/123456` (already correct)
- ✅ `https://civitai.com/models/123456/model-name` (model page)
- ✅ `https://civitai.com/models/123456?modelVersionId=789` (version page, with or without the name slug)
- ✅ `www.civitai.com` and `civitai.green` links
- ✅ `123456` (model ID only)
- ✅ Automatic search by model name for unrecognized URLs

## 📂 Project Structure

```
civitai-bulk-downloader/
├── 📁 civitai_downloader/     # Source package (installed by pip)
│   ├── 📁 api/               # CivitAI API client
│   ├── 📁 config/            # Configuration management
│   ├── 📁 downloader/        # Download engine
│   ├── 📁 preprocess/        # URL preprocessing
│   └── 📁 utils/             # Model management utilities
├── 📁 tests/                 # Comprehensive test suite
├── 📁 CSVs/                  # CSV files for batch downloads
├── 🐍 download.py            # Main CLI interface (civitai-download)
├── 🐍 preprocess.py          # Standalone URL preprocessor (civitai-preprocess)
├── 🐍 run_tests.py           # Test runner with coverage
├── ⚙️ config.json           # User configuration
├── 📄 pyproject.toml         # Package metadata and commands
├── 📄 requirements.txt       # Dependencies
└── 📄 requirements-test.txt  # Test dependencies
```

## 📊 CSV Format

Create CSV files in the `CSVs/` directory with this structure:

```csv
SrNo,Model_ID,Model_Name,Model_URL
1,4201,Realistic Vision V4.0,https://civitai.com/api/download/models/114367
2,12345,Another Model,https://civitai.com/models/12345/model-name
3,67890,Model with ID Only,67890
```

**Automatic CSV Generation**: Use the [CivitAI DownloadLink Extractor](https://github.com/deepratna-awale/CivitAI-DownloadLink-Extractor) to automatically generate CSV files.

## ⚙️ Configuration

The downloader creates a `config.json` file with customizable settings:

```json
{
  "api_key": "your-civitai-api-key",
  "csvs_directory": "CSVs",
  "model_paths": {
    "checkpoint": "models/Stable-diffusion",
    "lora": "models/Lora",
    "controlnet": "models/ControlNet",
    "vae": "models/VAE",
    "textualinversion": "embeddings",
    "upscaler": "models/ESRGAN"
  },
  "download_settings": {
    "max_concurrent_downloads": 4,
    "timeout_seconds": 300,
    "retry_attempts": 3,
    "chunk_size": 8192
  }
}
```

### Supported Model Types
- **checkpoint** → `models/Stable-diffusion/`
- **lora** → `models/Lora/`
- **locon** → `models/Lora/`
- **lycoris** → `models/Lora/`
- **controlnet** → `models/ControlNet/`
- **hypernetwork** → `models/hypernetworks/`
- **vae** → `models/VAE/`
- **textualinversion** → `embeddings/`
- **upscaler** → `models/ESRGAN/`
- **poses** → `models/Poses/`
- **other** → `models/Other/`

